h} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313771} :answer-field/id #uuid "78da5d84-405f-576d-a1d4-de283c4068e3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314330} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09893674-646d-5f37-bce4-59cd8beeafd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312046} {:answer/id #uuid "6cabb5e8-9525-5a91-ab0e-326c32158c07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312830} {:answer/id #uuid "7a27bfed-a2e7-5872-b949-87dffe1c91f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16{s}^{2}-24}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312951} {:answer/id #uuid "dc03fbb8-5a58-54bb-bdb8-59d4750b8cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24{s}^{2}-32}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09893674-646d-5f37-bce4-59cd8beeafd5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312046} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5715096-b5c8-55b9-a033-15fae14db265" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1112abd-9d76-5cb7-a3f0-3aa50fdea8d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-340850" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t$ and $F(s)=L{f(t)}.$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}={{field-2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\n{F}^{″}(s)={{field-3}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}{e}^{4t}}={{field-4}},\\,s>0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a function $f(t)$ is piecewise continuous on $[0,\\infty )$ and has exponential order $a,$ then its Laplace transform\n\n$$\nF(s)=L{f(t)}\n$$\n\nexists for every real $s>a,$ and $F$ is infinitely differentiable in this region of convergence. Moreover, for each integer $n\\ge 0$ and every such $s,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{n}f(t)}=(-1)^{n}{F}^{(n)}(s).\n$$\n\nIn particular, for $n=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={F}^{″}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that $f(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t.$ Using the given result with $\\omega =4,$ the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is \n\n$$\nF(s)=\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(4({s}^{2}+16)^{-1}) \\\\  & =-4({s}^{2}+16)^{-2}\\cdot 2s \\\\  & =-\\frac{8s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}} \\\\ {F}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{8s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{(s)^{′}\\cdot ({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-s\\cdot {(({s}^{2}+16)^{2})}^{′}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-s\\cdot 2({s}^{2}+16)\\cdot 2s}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{({s}^{2}+16)^{2}-4{s}^{2}({s}^{2}+16)}{({s}^{2}+16)^{4}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{{s}^{2}+16-4{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}) \\\\  & =-8\\cdot (\\frac{16-3{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the quotient rule to find ${F}^{″}(s).$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}={F}^{″}(s)=\\frac{24{s}^{2}-128}{({s}^{2}+16)^{3}},\\,s>0.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]
